sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Command File
    participant CP as Command Processor
    participant BS as Bed-Day Service
    participant PS as Pricing Service
    participant DS as Demand Service
    participant LE as Ledger Entry
    
    C->>CP: PARSE (COMMAND\|ts\|args)
    CP->>CP: Validate timestamp order
    CP->>BS: Check bed days (per admission)
    BS-->>CP: Post BED/NURSING lines
    CP->>PS: Calculate charge (category-at-event)
    PS-->>CP: Return gross, multiplier
    CP->>DS: Check demand trigger (>80% deposits)
    DS-->>CP: Return demand or None
    CP->>LE: Create ledger entry
    LE-->>CP: Return line_no
    CP-->>C: Command result (success/rejection)
